/* Partitioned overlap-save convolution, FP64.
 *
 * Structurally identical to fir_partition_f32.comp -- same bindings, same
 * push constants, same indexing, one invocation per (channel, bin) -- with
 * every buffer widened to dvec2 and the accumulation left uncompensated.
 * This is the double_precision profile without precise_fp64; the device must
 * report shaderFloat64, which fir_vulkan.c checks before selecting it.
 *
 * Bindings, in the order create_partition_pipeline() writes them:
 *   0 working  -- out: this block's accumulated spectrum.
 *   1 history  -- in: ring of the last `partitions` input spectra per channel.
 *   2 kernels  -- in: the transformed response, partition-major.
 *
 * Push constants (partition_parameters_t, 16 bytes): spectrum_bins,
 * partitions, channels, current_slot -- the last being the ring position of
 * the newest input block.
 *
 * Dispatch covers channels * spectrum_bins invocations rounded up to whole
 * workgroups of 256, hence the bounds test.
 *
 * (c) Simone Filippini <info@simonefilippini.it> 2026
